    description: "## Origin\n\nMaterialized 2026-06-04 from the 2026-06-03 fold-audit (Family F). Stand-alone finding F21.6 previously filed inline at the time of pass-21 (\"minor/standalone\" per the audit table). Initial context lives on INV-janob (filed 2026-06-01 as a face of INV-luhur) and on INV-luhur's pass-25 F25.5 substrate-verification entry.\n\nThe audit's verdict: F21.6 is STANDALONE because the producer/consumer name asymmetry — even if documented intentional — has concrete cost on consumer-side probes. Pass-26 F26.15 reframed this as \"documented intentional design\" (spec.md lines 260/1776) but the cost remains: consumers writing probes against `pass_id` or `origin_run_id` on AR records get silent-None and draw wrong conclusions.\n\n## Symptom\n\nAnalysisRun's producer-side identity field is named `execution_id` (84/84 ARs populate). The consumer-side FK pointing back to the AR carries a different name — `origin_run_id` on Node and Edge records (109915/109915 edges resolve; 32025/34253 nodes resolve via this FK; remaining 2228 are empty-string-sentinel cohort per INV-virik F25.4).\n\nDocumented intentional design per spec.md lines 260 / 717 / 1776 — but the cost is real:\n\n- Pass-25 probes Q5 / Q28 returned None for all 84 ARs because they used `ar.get('pass_id')` — `pass_id` is the conceptual alias; the actual JSON wire field is `pass`. Vacuous results, no exception raised, silent-wrong conclusions.\n- Pass-25 framed AR.origin_run_id as \"100% NULL on all 84 ARs\" — but AR doesn't have `origin_run_id` at all (it's a Node/Edge consumer-side FK name); `.get()` returned None for absence and the probe couldn't distinguish absence from null-value.\n\n## Invariant\n\nFor each producer/consumer naming asymmetry in the schema:\n\n1. spec.md explicitly documents the alias relationship at both surfaces (currently true for the 3 cases above, but the documentation is scattered).\n2. The conceptual name and JSON wire field are consistent within ONE surface (currently violated: agent-notes and spec narrative both use `pass_id` while JSON uses `pass`).\n3. Consumer-facing tools (htrac, probe scripts) document the alias explicitly OR resolve it automatically.\n\n## Fix sketch\n\n**Documentation-side fix (no code change).** Add a top-level table to spec.md or a new ADR documenting the 3+ known producer/consumer name aliases:\n\n| Producer | Consumer-FK | Conceptual | Wire field |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| AR.execution_id | Node.origin_run_id / Edge.origin_run_id | (run_id) | execution_id, origin_run_id |\n| AR.pass | (pass_id in agent-notes) | (pass_id) | pass |\n| AR.toolchain.grammar_module (`language_pack:*`) | rc.captured.grammars keys (`tree-sitter-*`) | grammar | language_pack:apex, tree-sitter-apex |\n\n**Schema-side fix (more invasive).** Rename `AR.pass → AR.pass_id` (the wire field follows the concept). Lower invasiveness option: add `pass_id` as an alias in the JSON output (writer emits both) while keeping `pass` for backward-compat.\n\n## Source provenance\n\n- **F21.6** — originally noted in pass-21 lab notebook (inline annotation; later cross-referenced by INV-janob).\n- **F25.5** — INV-luhur discussion entry 2026-06-02 (pass-25 batch); reframed by F26.15.\n- **F26.15** — INV-luhur discussion entry 2026-06-03 (pass-26 batch); documents the spec.md citations.\n\nLab notebooks: passes 21, 25, 26 under `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/`.\n\n## Related rows\n\n- **INV-janob** (face-only filing under INV-luhur — sibling row covering the AR.execution_id ↔ Node.origin_run_id naming asymmetry specifically).\n- Sibling: **INV-luhur** (META: meta-layer writer drift) — broader umbrella.\n- Sibling: **WI-language-catalogs-disjoint** (Family F — same shape: one fact, two surfaces, two namings).\n- Family F sibling rows."  # af5e
